From b102ba59ed44b229df5b8395d5a9db63f6ab62aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:27:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Hide CameraDeviceUserShim from the public SDK API
 surface

CameraDeviceUserShim is a pure internal Binder-interface implementation
detail (IInterface/ICameraDeviceUser is itself @hide), not real SDK
API, matching the rest of this restored HALv1 compatibility package.
Being non-hidden pulled its full method surface, including
getCaptureResultMetadataQueue()'s MQDescriptor<Byte, Byte> return
type, into current.txt, which frameworks/base's
systemfeatures-lookup-srcs generator's strict API-text parser can't
resolve (it requires fully-qualified non-java.lang types). @hide is a
documentation/stub-visibility annotation only; it has no effect on how
platform code calls this class at runtime.

Manually dropped the class's block from current.txt to match, since
regenerating it via 'm api-stubs-docs-non-updatable-update-current-api'
circularly depends on the same broken systemfeatures-lookup-srcs step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I8f8689158f394d346ea38ecc8589ae1f28ab9e1a
---
